            "text": "Alberto uses Claude across his AI agent work:\n\n- **Fraud Detection Agent** (deployed, for an online event ticketing platform): runs on Claude Haiku 5.5. On his reference set it reached 92% accuracy, approved 0% of fraud cases, and cost about $0.002 per review. It recommends approve, reject, or request-info, and a human admin makes the final call.\n- **Portfolio Agent** (this site): built with Claude and MCP. It answers visitors' questions about his experience and projects, and it is also exposed as an MCP server so external agents can query it. The source and eval report are public on GitHub.\n\nHis general approach includes offline evals that replay recorded cases in CI, measuring each change against the previous run, and tracking token budgets and costs. His AI stack also lists Grok and open-source models run locally via Ollama.",
